{"id":"sc900_p1_q001","exam":"SC-900","domain":"security_compliance_identity","objective":"security_compliance_concepts","subobjective":"shared responsibility model","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"An organization moves a web application from its own servers to a SaaS service. Which responsibility is most likely to remain with the customer?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Managing its users, data, and access settings"},{"id":"b","text":"Patching the SaaS platform's underlying operating system"},{"id":"c","text":"Maintaining the provider's physical datacenter"},{"id":"d","text":"Replacing failed storage hardware in the provider's facility"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"In SaaS, the provider operates the underlying infrastructure and platform, while the customer still manages responsibilities such as identities, data, and access configuration.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-concepts-methodologies/"],"tags":["shared responsibility","saas","shared_responsibility_model"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-concepts-methodologies/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-01","blueprint_leaf_id":"shared_responsibility_model","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-concepts-methodologies/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-security_compliance_concepts","semantic_family_id":"shared_responsibility_model","stem_style":"short_scenario","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q002","exam":"SC-900","domain":"security_compliance_identity","objective":"identity_concepts","subobjective":"authentication","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"A user enters a password and completes a biometric check before a resource evaluates what the user may do. What process is being performed first?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Authorization"},{"id":"b","text":"Authentication"},{"id":"c","text":"Federation"},{"id":"d","text":"Data classification"}],"correct_answer":"b","explanation":"Authentication verifies who the user is. Authorization is the separate step that determines what an authenticated identity is allowed to access.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-principles-concepts/"],"tags":["authentication","authorization","authentication"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-principles-concepts/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-01","blueprint_leaf_id":"authentication","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-principles-concepts/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-identity_concepts","semantic_family_id":"authentication","stem_style":"distinction_comparison","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q003","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_entra","objective":"entra_identity_types_and_function","subobjective":"entra id overview","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"Which Microsoft service is the cloud-based identity and access management service used to connect people to apps, devices, and data?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Microsoft Sentinel"},{"id":"b","text":"Microsoft Purview"},{"id":"c","text":"Microsoft Entra ID"},{"id":"d","text":"Azure Key Vault"}],"correct_answer":"c","explanation":"Microsoft Entra ID is Microsoft's cloud-based identity and access management service for connecting identities to applications, devices, and data.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-basic-services-identity-types/"],"tags":["entra id","entra_id_overview"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-basic-services-identity-types/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-01","blueprint_leaf_id":"entra_id_overview","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-basic-services-identity-types/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-entra_identity_types_and_function","semantic_family_id":"entra_id_overview","stem_style":"capability_selection","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q004","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_entra","objective":"entra_authentication","subobjective":"multifactor authentication","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"A sign-in policy requires a user to provide something they know and something they have. Which capability does this describe?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Single sign-on"},{"id":"b","text":"Federation"},{"id":"c","text":"Role-based access control"},{"id":"d","text":"Multifactor authentication"}],"correct_answer":"d","explanation":"Multifactor authentication requires verification using two or more factor categories, such as something you know and something you have.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-authentication-capabilities/"],"tags":["mfa","multifactor_authentication"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-authentication-capabilities/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-01","blueprint_leaf_id":"multifactor_authentication","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-authentication-capabilities/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-entra_authentication","semantic_family_id":"multifactor_authentication","stem_style":"direct_concept","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q005","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_entra","objective":"entra_identity_protection_governance","subobjective":"access reviews","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"A company wants resource owners to periodically confirm whether users still need access to a group and its applications. Which Microsoft Entra capability fits this requirement?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Access reviews"},{"id":"b","text":"Azure DDoS Protection"},{"id":"c","text":"Password protection"},{"id":"d","text":"Microsoft Sentinel analytics rules"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"Access reviews help organizations periodically review and recertify user access so unnecessary access can be removed.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-protection-governance-capabilities/"],"tags":["access reviews","governance","access_reviews"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-protection-governance-capabilities/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-01","blueprint_leaf_id":"access_reviews","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-protection-governance-capabilities/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-entra_identity_protection_governance","semantic_family_id":"access_reviews","stem_style":"short_scenario","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q006","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_infrastructure_security","subobjective":"azure key vault","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"An Azure workload needs a managed service for storing secrets, keys, and certificates rather than placing them in application code. Which service should it use?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Azure Bastion"},{"id":"b","text":"Azure Key Vault"},{"id":"c","text":"Azure DDoS Protection"},{"id":"d","text":"Network Security Groups"}],"correct_answer":"b","explanation":"Azure Key Vault is designed to safeguard cryptographic keys, secrets, and certificates used by applications and services.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"tags":["key vault","secrets","azure_key_vault"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-01","blueprint_leaf_id":"azure_key_vault","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_infrastructure_security","semantic_family_id":"azure_key_vault","stem_style":"capability_selection","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q007","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_security_management","subobjective":"microsoft defender for cloud","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"Which service brings together cloud security posture management and workload protection capabilities for cloud resources?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Microsoft Purview"},{"id":"b","text":"Microsoft Sentinel"},{"id":"c","text":"Microsoft Defender for Cloud"},{"id":"d","text":"Microsoft Entra ID"}],"correct_answer":"c","explanation":"Microsoft Defender for Cloud combines security posture management with cloud workload protection capabilities.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"],"tags":["defender for cloud","cspm","microsoft_defender_for_cloud"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-01","blueprint_leaf_id":"microsoft_defender_for_cloud","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_security_management","semantic_family_id":"microsoft_defender_for_cloud","stem_style":"capability_selection","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q008","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"defender_xdr","subobjective":"defender for endpoint","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"An organization wants detection, investigation, and protection capabilities focused on laptops and other endpoints. Which Microsoft Defender service is the best fit?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention"},{"id":"b","text":"Microsoft Defender for Identity"},{"id":"c","text":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365"},{"id":"d","text":"Microsoft Defender for Endpoint"}],"correct_answer":"d","explanation":"Microsoft Defender for Endpoint focuses on endpoint protection, detection, investigation, and response.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-threat-protection-with-microsoft-365-defender/"],"tags":["defender for endpoint","defender_for_endpoint"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-threat-protection-with-microsoft-365-defender/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-01","blueprint_leaf_id":"defender_for_endpoint","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-threat-protection-with-microsoft-365-defender/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-defender_xdr","semantic_family_id":"defender_for_endpoint","stem_style":"short_scenario","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q009","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_compliance_solutions","objective":"service_trust_privacy","subobjective":"service trust portal offerings","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"A compliance team needs Microsoft audit reports and information about how Microsoft cloud services meet standards and regulatory requirements. Where should the team look?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Service Trust Portal"},{"id":"b","text":"Microsoft Sentinel"},{"id":"c","text":"Azure Bastion"},{"id":"d","text":"Microsoft Entra ID Protection"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"The Service Trust Portal provides trust, compliance, and assurance resources about Microsoft cloud services, including audit and compliance documentation.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-compliance-management-capabilities-microsoft/"],"tags":["service trust portal","service_trust_portal_offerings"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-compliance-management-capabilities-microsoft/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-01","blueprint_leaf_id":"service_trust_portal_offerings","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-compliance-management-capabilities-microsoft/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-service_trust_privacy","semantic_family_id":"service_trust_portal_offerings","stem_style":"capability_selection","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
